This project is an unofficial Windows port and workbench for SUPRA-Tex.
It is not made or endorsed by the SUPRA-Tex authors.

The MIT License in LICENSE covers the code written for this project:
overlay/workbench/ (except overlay/workbench/web/vendor/), overlay/mesh_texture.py,
overlay/Setup-SUPRA-Tex.cmd, overlay/Start-SUPRA-Tex.cmd and the documents in docs/.
Third-party code keeps its own license, as listed below.

SUPRA-Tex
  Copyright (c) 2026 SUPRA-Tex Authors. MIT License (licenses/SUPRA-Tex-LICENSE.txt).
  https://github.com/Supra-3D/SUPRA-Tex
  overlay/supratex/inference/pipeline.py and overlay/supratex/pipelines/observation_guided_completion.py
  are modified copies of SUPRA-Tex files at commit cee4435652d0f23737bd28d5704e0fae9830b411.
  Changes: optional reduced precision (bf16/fp16) and GPU block streaming for low-VRAM cards.
  overlay/mesh_texture_test/ is made from the SUPRA-Tex pitcher_plant example
  (the mesh was moved, scaled and rotated for the install check).
  overlay/requirements-win-py314.txt is based on the SUPRA-Tex requirements
  (numpy and scipy versions changed for Python 3.14).

